{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# DNA Sequence Analysis using SentencePiece/BPE\n",
    "\n",
    "## Objective\n",
    "Demonstrate how **SentencePiece** (using Byte Pair Encoding) can automatically discover biologically meaningful DNA subsequences for species classification, compared to traditional fixed k-mer approaches.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Key Insight\n",
    "Unlike k-mers which use all possible fixed-length substrings, **BPE acts as an unsupervised pattern discovery tool** that learns variable-length patterns based on actual sequence statistics, similar to how compression algorithms work.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Dataset\n",
    "Kaggle DNA Classification Dataset: Human, Chimpanzee, and Dog gene sequences with 7 functional classes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup and Data Download"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install required packages\n",
    "!pip install sentencepiece pandas numpy scikit-learn matplotlib seaborn kaggle opendatasets"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import sentencepiece as spm\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from collections import Counter\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import classification_report, confusion_matrix, accuracy_score\n",
    "from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import CountVectorizer\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set style\n",
    "sns.set_style('whitegrid')\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (12, 6)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Download dataset from Kaggle\n",
    "import opendatasets as od\n",
    "\n",
    "# Download the dataset\n",
    "dataset_url = 'https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/miadul/dna-classification-dataset'\n",
    "od.download(dataset_url)\n",
    "\n",
    "# The data will be downloaded to './dna-classification-dataset/'"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load the datasets\n",
    "human = pd.read_table('./dna-classification-dataset/human.txt')\n",
    "chimp = pd.read_table('./dna-classification-dataset/chimpanzee.txt')\n",
    "dog = pd.read_table('./dna-classification-dataset/dog.txt')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add species identifier\n",
    "human['species'] = 'human'\n",
    "chimp['species'] = 'chimp'\n",
    "dog['species'] = 'dog'\n",
    "\n",
    "# Combine all data\n",
    "all_data = pd.concat([human, chimp, dog], ignore_index=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Total sequences: {len(all_data)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nClass distribution:\")\n",
    "print(all_data['class'].value_counts())\n",
    "print(f\"\\nSpecies distribution:\")\n",
    "print(all_data['species'].value_counts())\n",
    "print(f\"\\nSample sequence length: {len(all_data['sequence'].iloc[0])} bases\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nFirst sequence sample:\")\n",
    "print(all_data['sequence'].iloc[0][:100], '...')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Traditional Approach: K-mers\n",
    "\n",
    "**What are K-mers?**\n",
    "Fixed-length substrings of DNA sequences. For example, 6-mers extracts all 6-character substrings:\n",
    "- \"ACGTACGT\" → [\"ACGTAC\", \"CGTACG\", \"GTACGT\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "**Problem:** K-mers are arbitrarily fixed in length and don't adapt to biological patterns."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def getKmers(sequence, size=6):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Extract k-mers from a DNA sequence.\"\"\"\n",
    "    return [sequence[x:x+size].lower() for x in range(len(sequence) - size + 1)]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example\n",
    "sample_seq = all_data['sequence'].iloc[0]\n",
    "sample_kmers = getKmers(sample_seq, size=6)\n",
    "print(f\"Sample sequence: {sample_seq[:50]}...\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nFirst 10 6-mers: {sample_kmers[:10]}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTotal 6-mers in this sequence: {len(sample_kmers)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Extract k-mers for all sequences\n",
    "kmer_size = 6\n",
    "print(f\"Extracting {kmer_size}-mers...\")\n",
    "all_data['kmers'] = all_data['sequence'].apply(lambda x: getKmers(x, size=kmer_size))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Convert k-mers to strings for vectorization\n",
    "all_data['kmer_text'] = all_data['kmers'].apply(lambda x: ' '.join(x))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Done! Each sequence now has {kmer_size}-mers extracted.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create k-mer feature matrix using CountVectorizer\n",
    "print(\"Creating k-mer feature matrix...\")\n",
    "kmer_vectorizer = CountVectorizer(max_features=1500)\n",
    "X_kmer = kmer_vectorizer.fit_transform(all_data['kmer_text']).toarray()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"K-mer feature matrix shape: {X_kmer.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Using top {X_kmer.shape[1]} most frequent {kmer_size}-mers as features\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nExample k-mer features: {list(kmer_vectorizer.get_feature_names_out()[:10])}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. SentencePiece/BPE Approach\n",
    "\n",
    "**What is BPE?**\n",
    "Byte Pair Encoding is a compression algorithm that learns variable-length patterns based on frequency:\n",
    "- Starts with individual characters (A, C, G, T)\n",
    "- Iteratively merges the most frequent pairs\n",
    "- Learns patterns like \"CG\", \"TATA\", \"ACGT\", etc.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Advantage:** Discovers biologically meaningful patterns automatically!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Prepare data for SentencePiece training\n",
    "# SentencePiece expects one sequence per line in a text file\n",
    "with open('data/dna_sequences.txt', 'w') as f:\n",
    "    for seq in all_data['sequence']:\n",
    "        # Add spaces between each character so SentencePiece can work with DNA\n",
    "        spaced_seq = ' '.join(list(seq))\n",
    "        f.write(spaced_seq + '\\n')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Prepared {len(all_data)} sequences for SentencePiece training\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Train SentencePiece model\n",
    "vocab_size = 1500  # Similar to k-mer features for fair comparison\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Training SentencePiece model with vocabulary size {vocab_size}...\")\n",
    "spm.SentencePieceTrainer.train(\n",
    "    input='data/dna_sequences.txt',\n",
    "    model_prefix='models/dna_sp',\n",
    "    vocab_size=vocab_size,\n",
    "    model_type='bpe',  # Byte Pair Encoding\n",
    "    character_coverage=1.0,  # Cover all DNA characters\n",
    "    pad_id=0,\n",
    "    unk_id=1,\n",
    "    bos_id=2,\n",
    "    eos_id=3,\n",
    "    user_defined_symbols=['A', 'C', 'G', 'T']\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"SentencePiece model trained successfully!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load the trained model\n",
    "sp = spm.SentencePieceProcessor(model_file='models/dna_sp.model')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded SentencePiece model with {sp.get_piece_size()} pieces\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test on a sample sequence\n",
    "sample_seq = all_data['sequence'].iloc[0]\n",
    "spaced_sample = ' '.join(list(sample_seq))\n",
    "tokens = sp.encode(spaced_sample, out_type=str)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nSample sequence: {sample_seq[:50]}...\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nFirst 20 learned tokens: {tokens[:20]}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTotal tokens for this sequence: {len(tokens)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Compare to k-mers: {len(sample_kmers)} vs SentencePiece: {len(tokens)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Analyzing Learned Patterns\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's examine what patterns SentencePiece discovered!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Extract all learned pieces (vocabulary)\n",
    "learned_patterns = []\n",
    "for i in range(sp.get_piece_size()):\n",
    "    piece = sp.id_to_piece(i)\n",
    "    # Remove special tokens and spaces\n",
    "    if piece not in ['<unk>', '<s>', '</s>', '<pad>'] and '▁' not in piece:\n",
    "        clean_piece = piece.replace(' ', '')\n",
    "        if clean_piece and len(clean_piece) > 1:  # Only multi-character patterns\n",
    "            learned_patterns.append(clean_piece)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Discovered {len(learned_patterns)} multi-character patterns\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nPattern length distribution:\")\n",
    "lengths = [len(p) for p in learned_patterns]\n",
    "length_dist = Counter(lengths)\n",
    "for length, count in sorted(length_dist.items()):\n",
    "    print(f\"  {length}-character patterns: {count}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Show example patterns of different lengths\n",
    "print(\"\\nExample learned patterns by length:\\n\")\n",
    "for length in sorted(set(lengths))[:5]:  # Show first 5 lengths\n",
    "    patterns_of_length = [p for p in learned_patterns if len(p) == length]\n",
    "    print(f\"{length}-character patterns: {patterns_of_length[:10]}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize pattern length distribution\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "plt.bar(length_dist.keys(), length_dist.values(), color='steelblue', alpha=0.7)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Pattern Length (bases)', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Number of Patterns', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.title('Distribution of Learned DNA Pattern Lengths\\n(SentencePiece/BPE discovers variable-length patterns)', fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.grid(axis='y', alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.savefig('results/visualizations/pattern_length_distribution.png', dpi=300, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Average pattern length: {np.mean(lengths):.2f} bases\")\n",
    "print(f\"Longest pattern: {max(lengths)} bases\")\n",
    "print(f\"Shortest pattern: {min(lengths)} bases\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Find most common patterns across all sequences\n",
    "print(\"Finding most frequent patterns across all sequences...\")\n",
    "all_pattern_counts = Counter()\n",
    "\n",
    "for seq in all_data['sequence']:\n",
    "    spaced_seq = ' '.join(list(seq))\n",
    "    tokens = sp.encode(spaced_seq, out_type=str)\n",
    "    # Clean tokens\n",
    "    clean_tokens = [t.replace(' ', '') for t in tokens if t.replace(' ', '') and len(t.replace(' ', '')) > 1]\n",
    "    all_pattern_counts.update(clean_tokens)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nTop 20 most frequent learned patterns:\")\n",
    "for pattern, count in all_pattern_counts.most_common(20):\n",
    "    print(f\"  {pattern:15s} - appears {count:,} times\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Feature Extraction and Classification\n",
    "\n",
    "Now let's compare classification performance using k-mers vs SentencePiece features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Extract SentencePiece features for all sequences\n",
    "def encode_sequence_to_features(sequence, sp_model, vocab_size):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Convert a DNA sequence to a feature vector using SentencePiece.\"\"\"\n",
    "    spaced_seq = ' '.join(list(sequence))\n",
    "    token_ids = sp_model.encode(spaced_seq, out_type=int)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Create count vector (like bag-of-words)\n",
    "    feature_vector = np.zeros(vocab_size)\n",
    "    for token_id in token_ids:\n",
    "        if token_id < vocab_size:\n",
    "            feature_vector[token_id] += 1\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return feature_vector\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Extracting SentencePiece features...\")\n",
    "X_sp = np.array([encode_sequence_to_features(seq, sp, vocab_size) for seq in all_data['sequence']])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"SentencePiece feature matrix shape: {X_sp.shape}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Prepare labels\n",
    "y = all_data['class'].values\n",
    "\n",
    "# Split data for both approaches\n",
    "X_kmer_train, X_kmer_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X_kmer, y, test_size=0.2, random_state=42, stratify=y\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "X_sp_train, X_sp_test, _, _ = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X_sp, y, test_size=0.2, random_state=42, stratify=y\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Training set size: {len(y_train)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test set size: {len(y_test)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Train classifier using K-mers\n",
    "print(\"Training Random Forest with K-mer features...\")\n",
    "clf_kmer = RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=100, random_state=42, n_jobs=-1)\n",
    "clf_kmer.fit(X_kmer_train, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Predict and evaluate\n",
    "y_pred_kmer = clf_kmer.predict(X_kmer_test)\n",
    "acc_kmer = accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred_kmer)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nK-mer Approach Accuracy: {acc_kmer:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nClassification Report:\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred_kmer))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Train classifier using SentencePiece features\n",
    "print(\"Training Random Forest with SentencePiece features...\")\n",
    "clf_sp = RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=100, random_state=42, n_jobs=-1)\n",
    "clf_sp.fit(X_sp_train, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Predict and evaluate\n",
    "y_pred_sp = clf_sp.predict(X_sp_test)\n",
    "acc_sp = accuracy_score(y_test, y_pred_sp)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nSentencePiece Approach Accuracy: {acc_sp:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(\"\\nClassification Report:\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred_sp))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Compare performance\n",
    "print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*50)\n",
    "print(\"PERFORMANCE COMPARISON\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*50)\n",
    "print(f\"K-mer ({kmer_size}-mers) Accuracy:     {acc_kmer:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"SentencePiece/BPE Accuracy: {acc_sp:.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"\\nImprovement: {(acc_sp - acc_kmer)*100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*50)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize comparison\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(16, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "# K-mer confusion matrix\n",
    "cm_kmer = confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred_kmer)\n",
    "sns.heatmap(cm_kmer, annot=True, fmt='d', cmap='Blues', ax=axes[0])\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(f'K-mer Approach\\nAccuracy: {acc_kmer:.4f}', fontsize=14)\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel('Predicted')\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel('Actual')\n",
    "\n",
    "# SentencePiece confusion matrix\n",
    "cm_sp = confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred_sp)\n",
    "sns.heatmap(cm_sp, annot=True, fmt='d', cmap='Greens', ax=axes[1])\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(f'SentencePiece/BPE Approach\\nAccuracy: {acc_sp:.4f}', fontsize=14)\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel('Predicted')\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel('Actual')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('results/visualizations/confusion_matrices.png', dpi=300, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Pattern Discovery: What Did BPE Learn?\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's analyze which patterns are most important for classification."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Get feature importance from Random Forest\n",
    "feature_importance_sp = clf_sp.feature_importances_\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get top important token IDs\n",
    "top_n = 30\n",
    "top_indices = np.argsort(feature_importance_sp)[-top_n:][::-1]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Top {top_n} most important patterns for classification:\\n\")\n",
    "important_patterns = []\n",
    "for idx in top_indices:\n",
    "    pattern = sp.id_to_piece(idx).replace(' ', '')\n",
    "    importance = feature_importance_sp[idx]\n",
    "    if pattern and pattern not in ['<unk>', '<s>', '</s>', '<pad>']:\n",
    "        important_patterns.append((pattern, importance))\n",
    "        print(f\"{len(important_patterns):2d}. {pattern:15s} - Importance: {importance:.6f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Visualize feature importance\n",
    "patterns, importances = zip(*important_patterns[:20])\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 8))\n",
    "plt.barh(range(len(patterns)), importances, color='forestgreen', alpha=0.7)\n",
    "plt.yticks(range(len(patterns)), patterns, fontsize=11)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Feature Importance', fontsize=12)\n",
    "plt.title('Top 20 Most Important DNA Patterns for Classification\\n(Discovered by SentencePiece/BPE)', fontsize=14)\n",
    "plt.gca().invert_yaxis()\n",
    "plt.grid(axis='x', alpha=0.3)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.savefig('results/visualizations/top_patterns_importance.png', dpi=300, bbox_inches='tight')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Analyze patterns per species\n",
    "print(\"Analyzing pattern usage by species...\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "species_patterns = {}\n",
    "for species in ['human', 'chimp', 'dog']:\n",
    "    species_data = all_data[all_data['species'] == species]\n",
    "    species_counter = Counter()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    for seq in species_data['sequence']:\n",
    "        spaced_seq = ' '.join(list(seq))\n",
    "        tokens = sp.encode(spaced_seq, out_type=str)\n",
    "        clean_tokens = [t.replace(' ', '') for t in tokens if t.replace(' ', '') and len(t.replace(' ', '')) > 1]\n",
    "        species_counter.update(clean_tokens)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    species_patterns[species] = species_counter\n",
    "    print(f\"{species.capitalize()} - Top 10 patterns:\")\n",
    "    for pattern, count in species_counter.most_common(10):\n",
    "        print(f\"  {pattern:15s} - {count:,} times\")\n",
    "    print()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Compression Efficiency\n",
    "\n",
    "One key advantage of BPE is compression - representing sequences more efficiently."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate compression metrics\n",
    "sample_sequences = all_data['sequence'].sample(100, random_state=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "original_lengths = []\n",
    "kmer_counts = []\n",
    "sp_token_counts = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for seq in sample_sequences:\n",
    "    original_lengths.append(len(seq))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # K-mer count\n",
    "    kmers = getKmers(seq, size=kmer_size)\n",
    "    kmer_counts.append(len(kmers))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # SentencePiece token count\n",
    "    spaced_seq = ' '.join(list(seq))\n",
    "    tokens = sp.encode(spaced_seq, out_type=int)\n",
    "    sp_token_counts.append(len(tokens))\n",
    "\n",
